{#
  Admin "klant heeft gevalideerd" notification — ported from
  buildAdminValidatedHtml (send-pulse-mail.ts:172-183).
  NOTIF-01: cta_url is {app_base_url}/admin/pulse/intakes/{intake_id} — no token.
#}{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block tag %}Nestor Pulse — Admin{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<h1>Klant heeft gevalideerd</h1>
{#
  D-23.5-03. This line used to read
  `<strong>{{ client_name }}</strong> heeft de intake gevalideerd voor project "{{ project_title }}"`,
  which rendered the SAME value twice and labelled it as the validating party: the
  call site (`intake_routes._send_admin_validated`) passes `intake.client_name` to
  BOTH `client_name` and `project_title`, and `intakes.client_name` is the operator's
  free-text PROJECT label. So the mail said `Acme herpositionering heeft de intake
  gevalideerd voor project "Acme herpositionering"`. The actor is now named as "de
  klant" in prose and the value is rendered once, in the slot where it is true.
  `client_name` stays in `render_admin_validated`'s signature (jinja ignores unused
  context) so no caller and no test has to change; it is unrendered, not lost. When a
  real client/space name becomes available here, put it back in the actor slot.
#}
<p>De klant heeft de intake gevalideerd voor project &ldquo;<strong>{{ project_title }}</strong>&rdquo;.</p>
<p>Status: <code>validated_by_client</code></p>
<p>Volgende stap: Context Pack genereren en research starten.</p>
<p style="margin-top: 24px;"><a href="{{ cta_url }}" class="btn">Open intake in admin →</a></p>
{% endblock %}
